11	 *
12	 * `--stdout` prints the report instead of committing it, which is how to look at it
13	 * without touching the branch.
14	 *
15	 * ## Reading the sessions without a checkout
16	 *
17	 * `git show <ref>:<path>` per file, from the fetched ref. A worktree would put 25 MB on
18	 * disk to read files that are read once; and the current checkout at this point in a run
19	 * may hold the agent's own uncommitted work, which nothing here may disturb.
20	 */
